  "description": "Write C# for microcontrollers. RustNet compiles a .NET application to a compact RNX module, signs it, and runs it on an IL interpreter written in Rust — on ESP32, ESP32-C3, K210 (RISC-V), STM32, RP2040 and Meadow F7. This package is the managed API those applications are written against: GPIO/ADC/PWM/I2C, WiFi and MQTT, a display and UI toolkit, a filesystem, an embedded SQL database, field buses (CAN, Modbus, 1-Wire), serializers, and camera/USB support.",
